# Rendering of QFL/ert_coin_flip_{lb,ub}.qhes, P = 0.5 * 0 + 0.5 * (1 + P), whose least
# solution is 1: a tick is paid only on the flip that does not stop the loop.  A tick
# before the choice would pay every flip, an expected runtime of 2.
# The query is the upper source's bound P <= 1 as an expected-runtime bound; the source's
# P is the runtime from x = 0, and from any other x the loop does not run (runtime 0), so
# the bound 1 holds at every initial state exactly when it holds at x = 0.  The lower
# source, P >= 1, reads ?Ert [0] >= [x = 0] here.
nat x;

while(x = 0) {
	{x := 1}[0.5]{tick (1.0)};
}

?Ert [0] <= 1
